+| `WITH-STANDARD-IO-SYNTAX` | streams and I/O | `provider_gap` | ordinary text/resource state and finally / bracket / host I/O profile — Control scaffolding is reusable; exact CL stream/syntax state still needs a provider. No claim that a string Array alone implements every stream operation. L07. |
+| `WRITE` | printing and FORMAT | `provider_or_library_gap` | toLmx / formatInt / limited positional format / explicit text operations — These shorten serialization/display tasks, but full CL FORMAT directives, pretty-printer dispatch and readably round-tripping arbitrary Lisp objects are not implemented by positional format. L06. |
+| `WRITE-BYTE` | streams and I/O | `provider_gap` | ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider — Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07. |
+| `WRITE-CHAR` | streams and I/O | `provider_gap` | ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider — Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07. |
+| `WRITE-LINE` | streams and I/O | `provider_gap` | ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider — Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07. |
+| `WRITE-SEQUENCE` | streams and I/O | `provider_gap` | ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider — Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07. |
+| `WRITE-STRING` | streams and I/O | `provider_gap` | ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider — Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07. |
+| `WRITE-TO-STRING` | printing and FORMAT | `provider_or_library_gap` | toLmx / formatInt / limited positional format / explicit text operations — These shorten serialization/display tasks, but full CL FORMAT directives, pretty-printer dispatch and readably round-tripping arbitrary Lisp objects are not implemented by positional format. L06. |
+| `Y-OR-N-P` | interactive tools and debugging | `profile_or_metadata` | LMX observation/debugging contract and explicit host tooling — Interactive UI/debugger facilities are not algorithmic aliases. Runtime state inspection and stepping need real executor support; no transcript or inferred state is presented as execution. L13. |
+| `YES-OR-NO-P` | interactive tools and debugging | `profile_or_metadata` | LMX observation/debugging contract and explicit host tooling — Interactive UI/debugger facilities are not algorithmic aliases. Runtime state inspection and stepping need real executor support; no transcript or inferred state is presented as execution. L13. |
+| `ZEROP` | scalar arithmetic | `native_or_composition` | ordinary + - * / != < <= = > >= ** % and explicit numeric context — Use the native operation on the agreed numeric domain. CL MOD vs REM signs, division exactness, unary/variadic arity and overflow profiles must match; they are not silently identical. |
